# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Blazegraph test fixtures: tracked in git, but NOT hand-written source.
# Keep GitHub Linguist's language bar and diffs honest — fixtures are generated
# or vendored, so they must not count toward "what we wrote in".
# (CR-89 item B, 2026-07-14.)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Generated fixtures — golden anchors, cache tiers, emitted artifacts, stage
# snapshots. Machine-produced: exclude from language stats + collapse in diffs.
blazegraph-core/test_fixtures/**            linguist-generated=true

# Source documents we did NOT author (third-party inputs) → vendored, not
# generated. Later-matching rules override the broad line above per attribute.
blazegraph-core/test_fixtures/pdfs/**       linguist-generated=false linguist-vendored=true
blazegraph-core/test_fixtures/docx/**       linguist-generated=false linguist-vendored=true
blazegraph-core/test_fixtures/**/*.pdf      linguist-generated=false linguist-vendored=true

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LFS plumbing for FUTURE heavy fixtures — NOT active yet.
#
# git-lfs is not initialized in this repo, and existing fixtures stay in plain
# git on purpose: retrofitting them to LFS is a history rewrite, and
# trust-critical text (bgraph.md / config.yaml / PRODUCED_BY) must never hide
# behind an LFS pointer — the byte-honest golden freeze has to diff real bytes.
#
# When we stand up a bulk eval corpus, run `git lfs install` and uncomment,
# scoped to a NEW corpus path so existing blobs are never touched:
#
#   eval-corpus/**/*.pdf   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
#   eval-corpus/**/*.json  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
#   eval-corpus/**/*.docx  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
#
# (CR-89 item B / the LFS recommendation in the 2026-07-14 A/C/D session note.)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
